        "id": 5639,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-18T13:00:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think I’ve already mentioned the following opinions, which I believe are all solidly in the minority:</p>\n<p>[list]<br>\n[<em>]I don’t think the game needs scaling (though I appreciate the solution that someone offered of picking the number for H).[/</em>]<br>\n[<em>]I’m not interested in HP trackers. I enjoy using dice.[/</em>]<br>\n[<em>]I’m not interested in damage amount/type trackers. I don’t have the sense that they’ll help me very much.[/</em>]<br>\n[<em>]I don’t particularly care that the box can’t hold all of the cards. It’s a bit annoying, but the very inexpensive card boxes I’ve been using work great and<br>\nare readily expandable to handle more expansions.[/</em>][/list]</p>\n<p>My latest counterintuitive realization is that I don’t actually like the thicker card stock. Partly, I think, this is because having sleeved my cards I don’t think I notice the difference very much, but the other problem is that it takes up more space to have thicker cards. So, yes, my cheapo card boxes can be easily expanded to hold more cards, but now they have to be bigger and the box ends up weighing more than it otherwise would.</p>\n<p>All of these are rounding errors for me in the sense that I love the game and it none of this greatly increases or decreases my enjoyment.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:21.036Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
